  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## ☽'umbraum
    
    A Midnight Claws operative, known to his squad as **Umbra**, who served in the five-penguin unit assigned to guard the Obelisk — a pressure-blackened whale-bone artifact of contested provenance that ☽'umbraum called "the Bastard." His squadmates were Silvtasaevus~, Nanaiamis~, Velumia~, and Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane. He wore a bioluminescent-threaded cloak and carried himself with the easy physicality of someone raised in the deep tunnels, habitually leaning against the nearest structure as though the architecture owed him the favor.
    
    ☽'umbraum was, by all surviving accounts, a compulsive storyteller. His defining piece — a never-completed anecdote about "the time at Ravium~," referring to ☽'slew Ravium~, a contested deep-tunnel territory — was delivered in installments across multiple watches. His squad maintained he had been hiding behind a mineral pipe during the incident in question. He maintained he was strategically positioned. The dispute was never resolved. He used the compressed exhalation the Midnight Claws adopted in place of laughter, and by all accounts deployed it more freely the worse things became.
    
    ### Death at the Dawn Terrace
    
    During the orca assault on Terrace Momiou, ☽'umbraum took a crystal shard along his back while dragging the Obelisk across the second tier. The terrace floor — already compromised by harmonic damage from shattered spires — collapsed beneath him. He fell through to his midsection. A finisher orca positioned in the channel below killed him before the squad could intervene.
    
    He was partway through the Ravium~ story when the floor gave out. It never received a punchline.
    
    The ice-memory from Terrace Momiou, which I have referenced in my annotations on Augur ☽'Milucaum~, registered ☽'umbraum's thermal signature as the first of five to extinguish during the engagement. What followed his death — the forbidden blood-working, the violation of the Pactum∴ne accord — is documented under the entries for those who survived long enough to choose it.
