  annotation "note_1771594402204_0", anchor: "A finisher orca positioned in the channel below killed him before the squad could intervene.", text: "A finisher does not station itself beneath an intact terrace floor. Finishers hold escape routes — water exits, ice-shelf edges, the known breaking points. A channel beneath the second tier is none of these unless someone already knew the floor would fail. The harmonic damage from the spires provided the mechanism, but the positioning preceded the collapse. Either the orca mapped the terrace's structural tolerances in advance, or the spire destruction was not collateral but tactical — the assault creating its own kill zone. The standard accounts treat the floor giving out as bad luck. Orca raid doctrine does not rely on luck.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771594402204_1", anchor: "pressure-blackened whale-bone artifact of contested provenance", text: "'Contested' does too much work and I knew it when I wrote it. The provenance is not contested. It is suppressed. Three Nightshelf factions claim origin-rights; none will produce documentation. Whale-bone on the Berg means orca kill, which means someone retrieved it from waters no penguin enters voluntarily. The Claws knew whose bone it was. ☽'umbraum calling it 'the Bastard' was not irreverence — it was nomenclature.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771594402204_2", anchor: "hiding behind a mineral pipe during the incident in question", text: "☽'slew Ravium~ changed hands from The Cell to the Midnight Claws. Whatever happened behind that mineral pipe happened during a territorial seizure the Claws do not officially acknowledge conducting. No wonder he never finished the story.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
